<item><title>Angola has 370 mil people living with HIV, with fewer than half treated</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ao/angola-has-370-mil-people-living-with-hiv-with-fewer-than-0ce03a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ao/angola-has-370-mil-people-living-with-hiv-with-fewer-than-0ce03a/</guid><category>Angola</category><description>ANASO president António Coelho said 60% of Angolans living with HIV are aged 15 to 24, and that government struggles to get medicines to those who need them, with stigma.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:42:35 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ao/angola-has-370-mil-people-living-with-hiv-with-fewer-than-0ce03a/share.jpg" length="44081" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ao/angola-has-370-mil-people-living-with-hiv-with-fewer-than-0ce03a/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
